        "canonical_field": "essay:generated:workHistory.responsibilities.0",
        "expected": "At Summer Atlantic Capital / SAC Nexus, I own the machine-learning core of an anomaly-detection and alert-prioritization system. That includes the repository and CI scaffold, the event-ingestion pipeline, a versioned FastAPI microservice, and the public detection API. On the modeling side, I do temporal sequence modeling over event streams using RNN and Transformer-style approaches, anomaly scoring, and a learning-to-rank layer that decides which alerts an analyst should see first. I also built a retrieval-augmented LLM explanation layer so the system's outputs come with reasoning an analyst can actually check. A lot of my day-to-day responsibility is operational rather than purely modeling: an anomaly system that fires too often just creates a second problem, so I spend real time on prioritization quality, failure modes, and documentation. Previously, at Intelehealth, I was responsible for a resource-availability scoring pipeline in Python across 32 villages and for designing an evaluation framework comparing AI-generated clinical outputs against a 4,169-case clinical standard using stratified sampling.",
